            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="0901" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.77/3363: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-11T18:00:00-04:00">October 11, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1461. Reference Chinese operation of French Indochina-Yunnan railway
                    (Department’s 1230 and Embassy’s 1777 and 1865). French Committee here has again
                    informally approached Department. It appears that French employees of the
                    railway have been given notice <pb facs="0902" n="892" xml:id="pg892"/> by the
                    Chinese to vacate railway residences by October 31. In your discretion, you may
                    mention this situation casually to the Foreign Office and express an interest in
                    equitable treatment being accorded the French.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
